--TEST--
A route path capture declared `Core\Time\DateTime` is `E0752`, because its zone name holds a `/` a path cannot carry; its help names `#[Core\Query]` and `Instant`, and a `#[Core\Query]` value may be one — `rule:security/route-capture-is-laundered-by-its-type`
--FILE--
<?nvs
class Calendar {
    #[Core\Route(path: "/meetings/{starts}", method: Core\Http\Method::Get)]
    #[Core\Access(allow: Core\Audience::Public)]
    public function show(Core\Time\DateTime $starts): string {
        return $starts->toIso();
    }

    #[Core\Route(path: "/meetings", method: Core\Http\Method::Get)]
    #[Core\Access(allow: Core\Audience::Public)]
    public function list(#[Core\Query] Core\Time\DateTime $starts): string {
        return $starts->toIso();
    }
}
--EXPECT--

--EXPECTF-ERROR--
error[E0752]: `Core\Time\DateTime` is not a type `{starts}` can arrive at
  --> case.nvs:3:18
%A
  = help: a `DateTime` text has its zone name, such as `Europe/Vienna`, and a path cannot carry the `/` in it. Declare the parameter `#[Core\Query]`, or declare it `Core\Time\Instant`
%A
error: aborting due to 1 error
